-- title:
--   Eichler order locally maximal away from its level
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$, let $q,q'$ be primes, and let $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be the associated quaternion algebra. Assume [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ShimuraCurve.html#L20), that is: $a>0$ or $b>0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit precisely when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ which is an Eichler order of level $N\in\mathbb{N}$, i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\sqcap\Lambda_2'$ for some maximal orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2'$ (orders being submodules containing $1$, closed under multiplication, spanning $\mathbb{H}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and finitely generated, maximal meaning that every order containing them equals them), with relative index of the additive group of $R$ in that of $\Lambda_1$ equal to $N$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\neq q$, $\ell\neq q'$ and $\ell\nmid N$, let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell\in v$, and let $\Lambda_2$ be any maximal order of $\mathbb{H}$ with $R\leq\Lambda_2$. Then the two local boxes at $v$ coincide: the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda_2$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_v$ equals the corresponding subgroup built from $R$.
--
--   This is the local statement that an Eichler order of level $N$ is maximal at every place away from the level and from the ramification, so that its local completion cannot be shrunk by passing to a maximal order containing it. It feeds the indefinite level-raising step, where an Eichler order is compared with a maximal order after conjugation by a finite idele.
-- source:
